# Security

## Never commit or paste

- API keys, tokens, passwords, secrets
- Private user data
- `.env` files with real values

## Credentials

- Use environment variables (see `.env.example` for names only).
- Never hard-code `YOUTUBE_API_KEY`, LLM keys, DB passwords, or Langfuse keys.

## Agents and data

- Agents must not have unrestricted database access.
- Validate all tool inputs against schemas.
- Sanitize external / ingested data before persistence.
- Do not log secrets or PII in Langfuse or application logs.

## Portfolio integrity

- No Finary private APIs, logos, or proprietary datasets.
- Label synthetic data clearly; never claim it is production fintech data.
